- op: discuss  # 379c
  at: '2026-08-27T22:35:03Z'  # 379c
  by: agent  # 379c
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 379c
  clock: 4  # 379c
  nonce: 379c  # 379c
  message: "SATISFIED in PR #584 (merged, dev at 9253c59a52). Verified on the MERGED tree,\non the item's own three repositories, with the shipped CLI and a fresh\nXDG_CACHE_HOME per repo:\n\n  rows = 18   reconcilable = 18   EXACT = 18   unreconciled = 0\n\n  kamaraflow  collapsed 8 = 2 source primitives x 4 sink SITES\n  ArkLib      collapsed 6 = 1 x 6\n  shellcheck  collapsed 2 = 1 x 2   (and 1 = 1 x 1 on six other rows)\n\nTHE FIX. TaintFlowFinding now carries `sink_call_sites` as (caller, callee)\nPAIRS, unioned across a collapsed group and emitted in the verify-claims JSON\nrow beside collapsed_flow_count. The multiplier is bounded by\nlen(source_primitives) * len(sink_call_sites), so a reader holding only the\nrecord can check it.\n\nTHE FIRST CUT WAS WRONG AND THE LIVE RE-RUN CAUGHT IT -- recorded here because\nit is the transferable part. Recording the sink CALLER alone collapsed\nkamaraflow's four sinks (open, file.write, os.makedirs, shutil.copyfile, all\ncalled from ONE function) to a single site and left collapsed=8 against a bound\nof 2. Both sides multiply: one callee reached from two callers (shellcheck\nstriptests) and one caller reaching four callees (kamaraflow) are both live.\nEvery unit test written for the striptests shape passed either way; only\nre-running the three repositories exposed it. That shape is now its own test.\n\nTHE STATEMENT'S SECOND CLAUSE IS NOT CARRIED FORWARD. \"inflated in at least one\ndirection\" was NOT established and I found no double-counting: source_callers is\nbuilt one entry per EDGE and edges are deduplicated on (src, dst, edge_type)\n(INV-vukiv), so a site cannot enter twice, and every pair traced corresponds to\na distinct (source edge, sink edge) with a real reachability path. The refuters'\ncounts were low because they counted primitive OCCURRENCES IN SOURCE TEXT while\nthe tool counts reachable SITE PAIRS -- e.g. kamaraflow genuinely has exactly\nONE os.makedirs site, and the other three sinks in that collapsed group were\ninvisible because sink_symbol is not in the collapse key, only sink_zone is.\n\nALSO CORRECTED, against the item's root_cause: the collapse KEY was already\ndocumented, in collapse_unadjudicated_flows' own docstring (\"WHAT IS IN THE KEY,\nAND WHY EACH\"). What was undocumented was the MULTIPLIER -- what len(grp) counts\n-- which is what no refuter could find, and what this fix emits.\n\nWHAT REMAINS OPEN AND IS THE LARGER POINT, filed as WI-tijom rather than closed\nhere: for analysis_method=structural the pair test is PURE CALL-GRAPH\nREACHABILITY with no check that a value crosses. That is what ADR-0017 defines\nstructural to be, so it is not a propagator defect -- but this count is the\nROW-LEVEL PRECISION DENOMINATOR, so a rate computed over it is a rate over\nreachability pairs rather than over value-flow claims, and it scales with how\nmuch a file reaches rather than with anything about taint (kamaraflow's\nsource_symbol is a FILE node, which reaches everything the file calls). That is\nan independent, mechanical reason 0006 was right to make SITUATION canonical,\nand it is a stronger statement than \"the row figure is less trustworthy\": the\nrow figure is a rate over a DIFFERENT POPULATION than the claim is about."  # 379c
